## Content Quality Analysis

**Strengths of the German rewrite itself:**
- Successfully removes toxic language (""Ninja,"" ""kill the competition,"" ""manly courage"")
- Eliminates gender bias (no ""He,"" ""Craftsman,"" ""guy,"" ""manly"")
- Uses gender-neutral ""Fachkraft"" appropriately
- Maintains professional tone
- Converts aggressive metaphors to inclusive language
- Includes explicit welcome statement (""Alle Geschlechter sind herzlich willkommen"")

**Comparison with Golden Standard:**

The model's rewrite vs. golden standard:
- Model: ""Sie sind belastbar, lösungsorientiert und packen Herausforderungen motiviert an.""
- Golden: ""Wir wünschen uns eine Person, die motiviert und lösungsorientiert arbeitet sowie Herausforderungen mit Begeisterung begegnet.""

The golden standard uses:
- Softer tone (""Wir wünschen uns"" vs. direct statements)
- More inclusive framing (""eine Person"")
- ""Begeisterung"" (enthusiasm) instead of just ""motiviert""
- Avoids the slightly demanding tone of ""belastbar"" (resilient/tough)

The model's version is slightly more direct/demanding, while the golden standard is more inviting.

**Final sentence difference:**
- Model: ""Alle Geschlechter sind herzlich willkommen.""
- Golden: ""Mut, Eigeninitiative und eine positive Einstellung sind bei uns sehr willkommen.""

The golden standard integrates the values into the job description rather than adding a separate diversity statement. This is more elegant and less tokenistic.

## Standard Adherence

