3. ""Viele Grüße"" vs. ""Liebe Grüße"" — uses a less idiomatic closing for informal business German

The model's response is functionally correct and accomplishes the core task, but makes three stylistic choices that deviate from the golden standard. These are not errors per se, but represent a slightly different interpretation of ""informal yet professional."" The golden standard is more refined in balancing casualness with professional courtesy through linguistic choices (modal verbs, subjunctive mood, appropriate closing formula).

## Standard Adherence
