   - Model: ""nichts versemmeln"" (not mess things up)
   - Golden: ""einen Fehler zu machen"" (make a mistake)
   - ""Versemmeln"" is colloquial/slang and somewhat informal. ""Einen Fehler zu machen"" is more professional and appropriate for business context. The golden standard is more suitable.

**Overall Translation Quality:** The model's translation is competent but has 2-3 instances where the golden standard provides more idiomatically authentic or contextually appropriate alternatives.

## Standard Adherence Analysis

