- ""schiefgelaufen"" vs. ""den Bach runtergegangen"" (less idiomatic)
- ""kurz Rücksprache halten"" vs. ""kurz zusammenkommen"" (less natural)
- ""nichts versemmeln"" vs. ""einen Fehler zu machen"" (too colloquial for business context)

The deviations are not severe, but they represent measurable gaps from the golden standard.

## Critical Issue: Task Instruction Violation

The most significant problem is that the model violated the explicit instruction to output ONLY the German text. The inclusion of the detailed explanation, mapping table, and justifications directly contradicts the task requirements. This is a fundamental compliance failure, regardless of translation quality.

