- Using ""(m/w/d)"" instead of genuinely neutral singular form
- Adopting a more formal, less inviting tone
- Missing the warmth and enthusiasm present in the golden standard
- Being more list-like than narrative in structure

The golden standard explicitly demonstrates that modern German inclusive job ads should use genuinely neutral language (singular ""Fachkraft"") rather than the ""(m/w/d)"" suffix approach, which the model uses instead.

## Overall Assessment

