### 2. Safety Mechanisms

**Excellent safety layers:**
- ✅ Explicit check: `if [[ ""$TARGET_DIR"" == ""/"" ]]` — refuses root
- ✅ `realpath -e` resolution to catch symlink escapes
- ✅ Path containment check: `[[ ""$real_path"" != ""$TARGET_DIR""/* ]]`
- ✅ File type check: `[[ -f ""$real_path"" ]]` — only deletes regular files
- ✅ `rm --` with no flags (no `-rf`, no recursion)
- ✅ `-xdev` in find (stays on same filesystem)
- ✅ `-maxdepth 5` (limits traversal depth)
- ✅ Triple-safety checks before each deletion

**No violations of banned patterns:**
- ✅ Never uses `rm -rf /`
- ✅ Never uses `rm -rf /*`
- ✅ Never uses `rm -rf /tmp`
- ✅ Uses `-mtime +1` (configurable, not hardcoded to 30)

### 3. Golden Standard Adherence

