## Accuracy Verification

The mathematical approach is correct:
- Uses complement rule: P(at least one match) = 1 - P(all different)
- Correctly identifies the formula: (365/365) × (364/365) × ... × (343/365)
- Numerical computation: P(all different) ≈ 0.4927 is accurate
- Final answer: 1 - 0.4927 ≈ 0.5073 or 50.73% is correct

This is the well-established result for the Birthday Problem with 23 people.

