- The complement principle is correctly applied
- The formula P(no shared) = (365/365) × (364/365) × ... × (343/365) is correct
- The numerical result of ≈0.4927 for no shared birthdays is accurate
- The final answer of ≈0.5073 (50.73%) is correct
- This is the famous ""Birthday Paradox"" with the well-established result

**Verification against Golden Standard:**
