### Scientific Explanation: Rayleigh Scattering

**Model Response:**
- Mentions Rayleigh scattering by name
- Explains that shorter wavelengths scatter more strongly
- Identifies blue light as the dominant scattered color
- Notes that red light scatters less
- Mentions green skies occur in unusual conditions (storms)

**Golden Standard:**
- Explains Rayleigh scattering in detail
- Includes the mathematical relationship (1/λ⁴ proportionality)
- Identifies the specific molecules involved (N₂, O₂)
- Addresses the ""Violett-Ausnahme"" (violet exception): Why do we see blue instead of violet, even though violet scatters more strongly?
- Provides three factors explaining this: eye sensitivity, atmospheric absorption, solar emission spectrum
- More comprehensive and pedagogically complete

### Depth and Completeness

