- Correctly identifies this as the Birthday Problem
- Properly applies the complementary probability approach
- Correctly formulates: P(at least one shared) = 1 - P(all different)
- Correctly calculates P(no shared birthday) ≈ 0.4927
- Correctly derives final answer: 1 - 0.4927 ≈ 0.5073

