- High: 8 (Tight Coupling, Feature Envy, Primitive Obsession, Long Method, Arrow Code, Long Parameter List, Mixed Responsibilities)
- Medium: 7 (Magic Numbers, Duplicated Code, Dead Code, Switch Statement, Shotgun Surgery, Hardcoded Rules, Anemic Domain)
- Low: 1 (Conditional Complexity)

**Golden standard's severity distribution:**
- 🔴 Critical: 4 (God Object, Tight Coupling, Parameter-Signature-Mismatch, Temporal Coupling/Hidden State)
- 🟠 High: 10 (Arrow Code, Long Method, Duplicated Code, Long Parameter List, Inconsistent Return Types, Missing Error Handling, Feature Envy, Primitive Obsession, Magic Numbers, Missing Default Case)
- 🟡 Medium: 1 (Dead Code)

**Key difference:** The golden standard correctly identifies 4 CRITICAL issues (including 2 actual bugs), while the model only identifies 2 critical issues and misses the parameter-signature-mismatch and hidden-state bugs entirely.

